**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Economic Update — April 2022","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04-14","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/iran/publication/economic-update-april-2022","claim":"Iran's economy was recovering only gradually: just a third of pandemic-period job losses had been recovered, oil revenue shortfalls were widening the budget deficit, and sanctions, inefficiencies, and price distortions were still constraining growth.","locator":"Page text around lines 41-45","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous World Bank country update using official macro data and the Bank's Iran desk.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level macro context, not direct proof of Khamenei's personal action, but it frames the environment his regime governed.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says the oil sector and services were driving a gradual recovery, so the picture is mixed rather than uniformly negative."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran Economic Monitor, Spring 2022: Managing Economic Uncertainties","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/iran/publication/iran-economic-monitor-spring-2022","claim":"Higher oil and tax revenues improved the fiscal deficit ratio, but inflation was eroding low-income welfare; the report projected a 4.4 percent fiscal deficit for 2022-24 and recommended infrastructure investment, a better business environment, and well-targeted social safety transfers.","locator":"Report summary / special-focus overview","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank country-monitor summary; the page is a high-quality synthesis but the snippet is shorter than a full report excerpt.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published during 2022 and explicitly about the 2021/22 and 2022-24 outlook.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level context, not a direct Khamenei policy record; useful for the welfare and implementation environment under his rule.","contrary_evidence":["The same summary notes higher oil and tax revenues, so it is not a pure deterioration story."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"New World Bank Report Says MENA Labor Markets Need Level Playing Field","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-05-16","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/05/16/mena-labor-markets-need-level-playing-field","claim":"The report says many MENA economies lack contestable markets because state-owned enterprises dominate and receive preferential treatment in taxes, financing, and subsidies, while price controls and subsidies reduce incentives for private-sector participation.","locator":"Lines 152-165","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank press release summarizing a flagship report with direct policy findings; not Iran-specific at the micro level but clearly relevant to the region and Iran's structure.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Contemporaneous to 2022 and applicable as structural context for Iran.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context only; not Khamenei-specific, but it describes the market structure his regime oversaw.","contrary_evidence":["The report is regional rather than Iran-only, so it cannot by itself prove Iran-specific implementation or Khamenei's direct control."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Determinants of Inflation in Iran and Policies to Curb It","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-09-09","url":"https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/001/2022/181/article-A001-en.xml","claim":"The paper finds that fiscal deficits, currency depreciation, and sanctions drive inflation in Iran, and recommends gradual deficit reduction, stronger central-bank autonomy and accountability, and more private-sector competition, rule of law, and banking reform.","locator":"Abstract / summary and short-term priorities section","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF working paper on Iran-specific inflation drivers and policy options; it is research rather than a policy directive, but the diagnosis is explicit and contemporaneous.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Uses data through 2021 and was published in 2022, making it a strong near-period analytical source.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect policy context; it identifies the policy environment Khamenei controlled, but not a single ruler-order by itself.","contrary_evidence":["The paper is explanatory research, not a finding that Khamenei personally adopted the recommended reforms."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.5","5B.7","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's cost-of-living squeeze belies push for economic self-reliance","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters report)","publication_date":"2022-01-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/01/26/iran-nuclear-economy","claim":"Reuters reported that ordinary Iranians were facing a severe cost-of-living squeeze while official targets still called for 8 percent growth; the piece also described worsening economic hardship amid sanctions and mismanagement.","locator":"Lead paragraphs and quoted witness accounts","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on public economic conditions; it is not official data, but it is independent and close to the events.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to January 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The article reflects the regime's economic stance and reported public hardship, but it does not by itself isolate Khamenei's personal choice from the broader Raisi government.","contrary_evidence":["The article also notes that the state still publicly targeted 8 percent growth, so it shows aspiration as well as hardship."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's president approves public budget","publisher":"Business Recorder / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-31","url":"https://www.brecorder.com/news/40164199/irans-president-approves-public-budget","claim":"Iran's state budget targeted 8 percent growth and crude-oil sales of 1.2 million barrels per day despite continued U.S. sanctions.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters dispatch relayed by Business Recorder; the budget target is a concrete policy choice and is contemporaneous to 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to the Persian year beginning March 20, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The budget was approved by President Raisi's government, not personally by Khamenei, but it reflects the economic policy direction under his supremacy.","contrary_evidence":["A headline growth target does not show implementation, and the article itself notes continued U.S. sanctions."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Soaring bread prices spark protests and shop fires in Iran - IRNA","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters report)","publication_date":"2022-05-14","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/14/us-iran-protests","claim":"A cut in government subsidies for imported wheat triggered protests and flour-price hikes as high as 300 percent; the report also says official inflation was around 40 percent and that the government planned digital coupons for subsidized bread.","locator":"Lead paragraph / IRNA-reported details","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a specific policy shock and its immediate distributional consequences; the article gives concrete price-impact detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to May 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The subsidy cut was a government policy rather than a direct Khamenei order shown here, but it affected the population under his regime and is relevant to his economic stewardship.","contrary_evidence":["The government response included digital coupons, which is a mitigation measure rather than pure neglect."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran central bank governor blames protests for currency's fall","publisher":"MarketScreener / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-17","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Iran-central-bank-governor-blames-protests-for-currency-s-fall-42573774/","claim":"Reuters reported that Iran's central bank governor partly blamed anti-government unrest and U.S. sanctions for the rial's record lows and that the currency had lost nearly 20 percent of its value since the protests began.","locator":"Lines 959-977 of the Reuters text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Reuters reporting with specific market data and contemporaneous attribution from the central bank governor.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to December 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The currency shock reflects both policy and external pressure; the report does not isolate Khamenei's personal decision, but it is relevant to regime-level economic management.","contrary_evidence":["Sanctions and protest unrest are real confounders, so the currency fall cannot be attributed to domestic policy alone."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran Replaces Central Bank Chief As Currency Sinks Further","publisher":"RFE/RL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-currency-sinks-economy-lags-protests/32199012.html","claim":"Iran's government replaced the central bank chief as the rial kept falling; the new governor, Mohammad Reza Farzin, came from Bank Melli and the move was presented as an effort to contain rising prices in the foreign-exchange market.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting relayed by RFE/RL; the personnel change is concrete, but the ruler-level link is indirect because the cabinet made the appointment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to late December 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Weak-to-indirect. This is a cabinet-level appointment under Raisi, not a proven Khamenei order; useful mainly as regime-context on technocratic response.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not show that the new appointment solved the currency problem, and it may simply reflect crisis reaction."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Development Indicators DataBank - Gini Index for Iran","publisher":"World Bank DataBank","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://databank.worldbank.org/reports.aspx?country=IRN%2CKIR&series=SI.POV.GINI&source=2","claim":"The World Bank DataBank table shows Iran's Gini index at 34.8 in 2022.","locator":"DataBank table, 2022 column","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank distribution indicator with a directly visible annual table entry.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The table includes the 2022 value directly, so the period fit is exact.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level inequality context, not direct proof of Khamenei's policy choice.","contrary_evidence":["A Gini value alone does not show who caused the distributional pattern or whether any policy improved it."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"سیاست‌های کلی برنامه پنج ساله هفتم","publisher":"nezamat.ir","publication_date":"2022-09-12","url":"https://nezamat.ir/post-43938/","claim":"The Persian-language reproduction of Khamenei's seventh development-plan guidelines sets economic progress with justice as the main goal, targets an average 8 percent growth rate, calls for single-digit inflation over five years, and directs liquidity and bank credit toward productive activities rather than non-productive ones.","locator":"Persian bullet points under اقتصادی","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local-language reproduction of the decree's wording; the host site is secondary, but the text is specific and clearly attributed to the Supreme Leader's guidelines.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to September 2022 and explicitly about the next five-year plan.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Supreme Leader guideline, though hosted on a secondary Persian site rather than the original office domain.","contrary_evidence":["This is a planning decree, not proof that the targets were met in practice."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I screened roughly 30 documents across World Bank Iran monitors, IMF country and working-paper material, Reuters/Euronews reporting, World Bank data tables, and Iranian/Persian-language policy reproductions.
- I kept the World Bank April 2022 and Spring 2022 Iran monitors because they give the strongest 2022 macro baseline, jobs, inflation, and welfare context.
- I kept the IMF inflation paper because it is the clearest Iran-specific analytical source on why inflation was high and what reforms would matter.
- I kept the World Bank MENA labor-market report because it gives the cleanest statement on state-owned enterprises, preferential treatment, and the private-sector level-playing-field problem.
- I kept the Reuters budget, bread-price, currency, and central-bank stories because they provide concrete 2022 policy actions and household effects.
- I kept the World Bank DataBank Gini table because it gives a direct 2022 inequality datapoint.
- I kept the Persian-language seventh-plan decree reproduction because it is the best local-language evidence for Khamenei's stated economic priorities in 2022.
- I rejected or collapsed multiple duplicates of the same March 2022 Khamenei speech, multiple syndicated copies of the bread-subsidy and currency stories, and general IMF methodology pages that did not add Iran-specific evidence.
- I also set aside later 2024-2025 poverty briefs and 2026 war-era news because they were out of period for the 2022 chapter, even when they were informative about longer-run trends.
- I did not keep older 2017-2021 IMF financial-sector papers as target-year evidence; they remain useful only as inherited-baseline background, not 2022 ruler-period proof.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct ruler-attributed evidence on economic appointments is still thin. The record shows a cabinet-level central-bank reshuffle and general policy direction, but not a clean Khamenei-specific personnel choice in 2022.
- Household welfare is better evidenced than ruler attribution, but a stronger 2022 poverty micro-series for Iran would help, especially for regional and gender distribution.
- Evidence on anti-corruption, monopoly power, and bonyad/IRGC-linked capture under Khamenei in 2022 is still mostly structural rather than ruler-specific.
- The strongest missing piece for a higher-confidence judgment is implementation evidence: whether the 7th development-plan targets, tax-financing shift, and productive-credit directives were actually carried out in 2022 rather than remaining slogans.
- More search would help, especially in Persian, if you want to tighten 5B.2 and 5B.5 rather than relying on macro context plus ruler rhetoric.
